# Skill integrity is a hash over file bytes, and the git registry serves working-copy
# bytes from a clone — so checkouts must be byte-identical on every platform. Forcing LF
# overrides core.autocrlf on the user's machine; without this, a Windows clone checks out
# CRLF and every install fails its integrity check.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Validation captures are hashed as recorded, including their original line endings.
# Preserve their bytes when staging and checking out the archived evidence.
docs/skill-validation/**/*.txt -text
